      "message": "Good point. I tried that first. The local nested class is also named FakeHttpServletRequest, so adding\n\n```\nimport com.google.gerrit.util.http.testutil.FakeHttpServletRequest;\n```\n\ndoesn\u0027t help: the import is shadowed by the local declaration in the same file, and `extends FakeHttpServletRequest` would then resolve to the local class (illegal self-extension).\n\nTwo ways to avoid the inline FQN:\n\n* (a) rename the local class (e.g. ProjectQoSFakeRequest);\n* (b) keep the FQN at the single `extends` site.\n\nI went with (b) since the parent type is referenced exactly once in this file and (a) would churn the rest of the test for a stylistic gain. Happy to switch to (a) if you\u0027d prefer — just wanted to flag the shadowing constraint so the trade-off is visible.",
